us per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-nine-way-hub"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-nine-way-hub"],"id":"long.thm-nine-way-hub","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.32 (Equivalent descriptions of half-membership)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.32, p. 53, label thm:nine-way-hub","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Each of the following is equivalent to $1/2\\in\\mathcal A$:*\n\n1.  *The integer-greedy sequence is not eventually always on branch $\\mathrm R$.*\n\n2.  *There are arbitrarily large $s\\ge5$ with $s\\notin D_{s+1}$.*\n\n3.  *Upper or middle transitions occur at arbitrarily large rows.*\n\n4.  *Some sequence $s_j\\to\\infty$ satisfies $s_j\\notin D_{s_j+1}$ for every $j$.*\n\n5.  *There are rows $s_j\\to\\infty$ and omitted ranks $d_j\\in\\{2,\\ldots,s_j-1\\}\\smallsetminus D_{s_j}$ with $d_j\\to\\infty$.*\n\n6.  *The positive ranks omitted by the real half-greedy rule form an infinite set.*\n\n7.  *The real half-greedy rule has no last omitted positive rank.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-nine-way-hub","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-nine-way-hub","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-nine-way-hub%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.half_mem_mersenneAchievementSet_iff_cofinalTerminalFalse%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-nine-way-hub%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.half_mem_mersenneAchievementSet_iff_cofinalTerminalFalse%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.half_mem_mersenneAchievementSet_iff